              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to stop, then the Mandarin for to leave a place."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 试",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "试 — shì — \"to try; to try on\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "这个能试吗 zhège néng shì ma — Can I try this one on?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 试 (shì) — the speech piece of 说 on the left; on the right six strokes: a horizontal across the top, a small three-stroke piece low under it, and a long stroke that slants down and hooks, with a dot at its top right. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "试 (shì) is inherited from Middle Chinese syiH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'to use'. Trying a thing by putting it to use is the usual explanation, but the step is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking for what I want."
            }
          ]
        },
